<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lê Uy Mục</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1488–1509</span> · Also known as Le Uy Muc</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lê Uy Mục was emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> of the Later Lê dynasty from 1505 to 1509, remembered as a cruel and dissolute ruler. He purged members of the royal family and officials, and was overthrown and killed in 1509 by his cousin, who reigned as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-tuong-duc">Lê Tương Dực</a>.</p></div>
